      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. so if we treat the intensity as a latent variable, we can basically use it to calibrate the jump component of the model. i've noticed that the higher the intensity, the larger the jump magnitude usually is. if we were to design a Bayesian framework where my \"spike\" provides a prior for the jump probability, how would we go about structuring the likelihood function to account for the time-lag between my signal and the market's reaction? i want to see if we can actually turn this into a predictive tool for high-frequency scenarios.",
